+ MarkupAttachment

` Linked nodes retain their owner through retained-host so the attachment tree is the structural
` ownership tree. A publicly adopted parentless non-root leaf instead uses the same attachment as
` a cleanup payload: retained-host is cleared, and the scalar object/witness pair reconstructs the
` interface only while client code still holds the owner. Adding its first structural child moves
` it back to ordinary ownership. Generated regions mount parentless only transiently and remain
` ordinary payloads until their builder links them.

+ object-address Size = 0
+ host-witness-address Size = 0
+ retained-host MarkupElement?
+ is-cleanup-payload = false
+ store-address Size = 0
+ store-witness-address Size = 0
+ retained-store MarkupRootElement?
+ mounted-parent MarkupAttachment?
+ mounted-callback-fired = false
+ is-released = false
+ is-closed = false
+ structural-parent MarkupAttachment?
+ first-child MarkupAttachment?
+ last-child MarkupAttachment?
+ previous-sibling MarkupAttachment?
+ next-sibling MarkupAttachment?
+ is-style-shadow = false
+ attachment-id Index = 0
+ style-store-address Size = 0
+ style-node-record-address Size = 0
+ dirty-bits U32
+ pending-domains U32
+ descendant-domains U32
+ generation U32
+ style-settled = false
+ style-reports-settle = false
+ cause = markup-cause-none
+ object-pointer => object-address as Pointer
+ is-live => style-store-address != 0
+ owner-address => object-address

_ overflow MarkupAttachmentOverflow?

